{"id": "EUVD-2026-98946", "enisaUuid": "f996c82d-561b-3438-bb67-8252fe7d01c3", "description": "Risesoft Digital-Infrastructure 9.6.5 through 9.6.11 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the fileManager Y9FileController.retrieveFileStream handler that allows unauthenticated attackers to read arbitrary files by supplying parent-directory segments in the fullPath and fileName parameters. Attackers can request the unauthenticated /rest/retrieveFileStream endpoint to retrieve files like application.yml, exposing database, Redis and Nacos credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T16:53:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T15:58:57", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@1ExmmukzRMWN7B4gQ4W-4Q/digital-infrastructure-filemanager-path-traversal-rw", "https://github.com/risesoft-y9/Digital-Infrastructure/blob/v9.6.11/y9-digitalbase-module/y9-module-filemanager/risenet-y9boot-webapp-filemanager/src/main/java/net/risesoft/y9public/controller/Y9FileController.java#L136-L166", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/digital-infrastructure-9.6.5-through-9.6.11-path-traversal-via-filemanager-retrievefilestream"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qqmw-cvh2-5395", "CVE-2026-110115"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "5ea7adab-4970-3bcf-a56a-4e7ea2c3244d", "product": {"name": "Digital-Infrastructure", "vendor": {"name": "risesoft-y9"}}, "product_version": "9.6.5 \u22649.6.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e5648ecc-2912-3a66-ae56-48c7374c155b", "vendor": {"name": "risesoft-y9"}}], "isExploited": false}